\ul Furthermore:\ulnone\line\line\tab The navigation tree no longer shows previews of Icons or Icon groups properly like it should. Only the Root node of the section should have our custom Icon displayed. the actual items in the tree below those sections should be displaying their actual Icon. For the Dialogs section I would like it to work like resource hacker and at the very least allow you to click a button to preview the dialog. Though ideally I would also like to be able to graphically edit them too. When viewing the text for the "Version Info" it displays text weirdly and has broken characters like this "\f1\u16385?\f0\u7600??" on occasion. it also should have line numbers for script sections and not wrap text between lines as this would break them if you try to compile it after. The "Extract Monolithic" option does not do what I intended. it should allow me to literally extract EVERY SINGLE ITEM as the correct file type into a directory of my choice using sub folders corresponding with the node they came from so all Icons from the "Icon Groups" section would be in a folder within the directory I specified after clicking the menu item called "Icon Groups" and same for all the others all the BMP bitmap images would be in their own folder ect. as actual correct files (We would obviously ignore the "Icons" Section as this would be taken care of by the icon groups. I dont want a bunch of ico files for each size and color depth the single ico groups for each set of icons is perfectly fine. I also want to be able to right click on any given node and simply extract all items in that node of a specified type. so All Icons or all Bitmaps without having to extract the entire thing. Currently the Export Monolithic option just saves a broken dll or exe file that no longer works for some reason. In the action menubar menu the menu options dont do anything and I am confused as to why there are separate ones for each type considering it would have no idea WHICH bitmap, Icon, Cursor or Other resource its replacing? I could be wrong it just needs to be more clear, Oh! And Actually function! lol. Also add from resource script res / rc does nothing as well. \line\line\tab When saving it should automatically rename the original file to append ".1.bak" ".2.bak" ".3.bak" before saving the new version. and continue counting up until a number is available. So save initiates a rename of the original then saves a new copy of the modified version with the original file name once the originals are safely baked up. \line\line\tab I would like to be able to have a viewer tab that acts like a file browser showing you icon sized previews of a selected tree node. \par
\tab Rename the button from "Test Imageres" and instead name it "Demo File!" and instead of imageres.dll can you actually make it target shell32.mun inside the systemResources Folder. I relocated the project so the paths to the original are broken. also when you click that button I want it to make a copy of that file and place it in the same directory as the program is running from THEN open that copy not the original (As its an example file I dont want people to accidentally break their system if they dont understand what they are doing!)\line\line\tab When replacing image assets I want to be able to use any file format and have the program automatically convert files between png bmp ico jpeg jpg ect. So for instance if I took a plain PNG and wanted to replace an Icon with that png, the software would in the background take that image use it as the largest icon inside that icon group, and scale the image to 16x16 24x24 32x32 48x48 64x64 96x96 128x128 256x256 using the original or as close to it as the largest size and scaling down unless the image is smaller than 256x256. In that case it would have to also scale up to make all those sizes. thus creating a standard icon container ico file. for bmp images it should do its best to remove the background eg. pink, gray, black. which sometimes happens to bmp images after exporting them elsewhere. \par
\tab Settings dialog window should have the exact same banner color gradient as the main window and also the layout is clipping you can safely move the check boxes up as well as the field for custom cert. (When we actually start coding... After we layout the plan!!)\par

